WEBVTT

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.220
He seems to be finishing up nicely.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.210
Well, he's become very motivated,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.970
to be in the best possible condition when he fights Joe Yabuki.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:09.940
H-Henry!

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.190
Hey.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.910
Who is that?

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.740
This is Henry James, an old friend of mine.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.240
He's a boxing promoter.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.450
A promoter?

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.160
What brings you here to us uninvited?

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:33.170
They don't call me Henry the Hyena for nothing. I show up whenever I smell a profit.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.300
A profit?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.390
Yes.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.890
I'd like to talk to you, Robert.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.100
Okay.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.270
It's been so long...

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.460
So, Robert, how long do you plan on staying here?

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.750
You're not living up to your name of Robert the Moneymaker.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.840
Oh, we're only getting started in Japan.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.750
We still have our match with Joe Yabuki.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.630
Joe Yabuki?

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.930
Well, I don't know how great this Joe Yabuki is,

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.760
but he can't possibly be greater than José Mendoza.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.760
José Mendoza? As in the world champion?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.730
Yeah.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.890
Is that why you're-

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.770
That's right. I've come to give you and Carlos some good news.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.270
You mean a world title match between Carlos and Mendoza...

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.200
That's right. And if you're interested, now's your best chance.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.280
Might even be your only chance.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.410
To be the world champion...

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.000
As he is now, Carlos can attain the title.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.410
Then that'll make you the champion's manager.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.250
What do you say? Wanna leave for America with me right now?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.260
Is that all you have to say?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.470
Pull over.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.800
Hey, is this deal not sweet enough for you?

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.800
I said pull over!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.320
I'm sorry, but I'm going home now.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.490
Hey, what's gotten into you, Robert? What are you thinking?

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.440
I'm only surprised because it's so sudden.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.530
There's nothing to think about!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.240
Or don't you want to make Carlos the world champion?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.120
Of course I do!

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.500
But now he's on fire to face Yabuki!

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.910
And I don't want to put that fight out!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.380
You're a bigger baby than I thought!

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.630
It's a match against some nobody named 
Yabuki versus an actual world title match.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.930
What's there to think about?

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.760
You might not get another chance!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.350
Do you want to take this chance and drive down the sunny highway,

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:55.520
or do you want to keep on crawling through the slums as the uncrowned emperor?

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.860
Well, get some fresh air and think about it a bit.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.910
I'll see you again soon.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.820
<i>Do you want to take this chance and drive down the sunny highway,</i>

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:50.370
<i>or do you want to keep on crawling through the slums as the uncrowned emperor?</i>

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.250
<i>Well, get some fresh air and think about it a bit.</i>

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.130
The sunny highway...

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:59.710
Carlos and I have been doing everything we can to crawl our way out of the slums to get on it!

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.300
That's our goal!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.800
And we've finally been given that chance!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.610
Hey, keep it steady! I can't write straight!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.610
Like you could write straight to begin with!

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.610
Yeah, Joe! Your handwriting's the worst!

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.120
I know you haven't gone to school or anything,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.700
but that just looks like chicken scratches!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:31.660
Shut up!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.580
I thought you were supposed to wipe the windows!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:41.080
And just what do you think you're doing?

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.920
Hey, old man!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.130
What do you think? Take a look!

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.090
Tange Gym finally has its own private vehicle!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.090
Isn't that Hayashi-san's van?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:55.100
Yeah, that's right, it was! Hayashi donated it to us!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:59.650
I guess business must be good for Hayashi-san, if he's getting rid of this good a car!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.780
Mammoth's been working really hard,

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.570
so Hayashi bought a new van to replace this one!

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.400
What do you say, old man?

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.820
Want a test drive around the block?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.660
Yeah! All right! Awesome!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.750
What's the matter, old man?

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.620
I know how to drive!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.330
They taught me back in juvie.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.000
What about your training?

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.670
My training?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.670
I did my fill of it, enough to drench two other shirts in sweat.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.170
Joe, who's your opponent again?

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.180
Who? The world-ranked boxer, Carlos Rivera, of course.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.270
So you do know.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.480
Then I have nothing to say to you.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:41.570
But are you sure that going through three shirts is enough training?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.400
Well, looks like the old man's in a bad mood.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.700
You'd better get on home.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.190
What the hell!? That's not fair!

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:53.200
Yeah! We helped you repair the van because you promised us a test drive!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.660
Just be patient! We've always got tomorrow. Okay?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.460
<i>Yeah, what's the deal!?</i>

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.500
Liar! I'm never helping you again! Never ever!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.670
He's right. I can't spend all my time doing this.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.350
After all, I'm up against...

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.480
What did you just say?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.900
You want Carlos to fight a world title match?

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.200
This must be that promoter Henry's suggestion.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.820
Then what about his match with Yabuki Joe?

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.460
We haven't signed anything yet!

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.040
There's still time to turn it down!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.330
Do you think Carlos truly desires to be the world champion now?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.750
Yes, of course he does!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:49.180
There's not a single boxer out there who wouldn't want the championship belt!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.570
What's up, Robert? You look pale.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.270
And you seem in a good mood.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.860
Of course. I can't help but feel excited when I think about my match with Yabuki.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.830
Carl-

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:17.910
Carlos, what if...

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.700
we had to cancel your match with Yabuki?

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.200
What!?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.670
Oh, it's only hypothetical.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:28.210
What if there was a match more important to us than your match with Yabuki?

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.430
Don't start putting "what if" situations in my head.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.640
All I can think about now is my match against Yabuki.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.680
I don't want to think about anything else.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:00.030
Well, hello, Robert! Been on the sauce, have you?

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.790
Henry, please just go home...

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.040
Stop troubling us...

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.920
Troubling you? Far from it! I thought you'd be happy!

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.050
Yes, I am happy. And that's what's troubling me.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.050
I take it Carlos said no?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.600
No, I just couldn't tell him.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.600
But he got really sour at me when I tried to tell him indirectly.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.060
I see. Sounds just like the Carlos I know.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.860
But Robert, it takes two to have a match.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.070
No matter how motivated Carlos is.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.610
R-Right.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.070
What if,

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.780
and only if, his opponent Joe Yabuki refused?

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.570
How do you think Carlos would react?

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.460
There's more than one way to skin a cat, Robert.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.990
Yeah! That's the way!

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.000
Do some jabs!

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.170
One-two! One-two!

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.720
All right! Way to go!

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.150
Yeah, go, go! Uppercut!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.870
Oh, sweet! It's a foreign car!

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.780
This thing must be a Plymouth!

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.250
Robert?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.120
Hey, Joe!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.210
What's this? You here to snoop around before the big match?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.260
Oh, no, no! I wouldn't need to observe you again at this point!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.390
Who's the guy with the jewelry?

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.430
Let me introduce him to you.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.140
Hey, Henry!

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.020
The name's Henry James.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.140
I'm a boxing promoter.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.350
Nice to meet you.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.400
A promoter?

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.980
Hold it! Business before the handshake.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.940
So what brings you to this broken-down old gym?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.490
As a matter of fact, Henry wants to make your gym a better one.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.490
<i>A better one?</i>

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:04.990
That's right. Isn't this a humble gym for a promising young fighter like yourself?

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:08.120
If possible, he doesn't mind hiring you for his own gym...

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.790
Now that's funny.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.620
So the great Yabuki Joe finally gets his big break?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.550
Yes, that sounds about right.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:15.630
What do you say, Joe?

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.510
Don't get cocky now, Robert.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.140
If you think you can bribe me with money, you're dead wrong!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.980
Oh, we're not bribing anybody! This is genuine kindness!

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.890
Genuine, my ass! This is dirty!

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.350
Why not just ask me to throw the fight, Robert?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.400
Oh, you've got the wrong idea entirely!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.540
Then what do you want?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.950
I guess we have no choice but to tell you the truth.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:49.330
We want you to forget any and all plans to fight Carlos.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.830
What was that!?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.790
I don't know how else I can put it...

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.090
I know. We want you to withdraw from the deal.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.590
I see.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.090
So you're getting scared now that the match is coming up.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.220
You want out, do you?

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.810
You want to quit in order to avoid the shame of losing!

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:07.300
Am I right?

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.770
Interpret it however you wish.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:12.310
As long as you'll cancel the match...

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.400
Oh, I see...

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.600
is what I'd like to say, but...

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.350
That's not gonna happen!

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.240
Well, am I wrong?

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.280
You've been leading me along this whole time...

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.440
You can't tell me to quit now!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.450
So you refuse?

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.330
Go back and tell Carlos that I said:

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.960
"The only way to put out Yabuki Joe's flame is to fight him in the ring!"

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:31.830
Joe!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.450
Shut up! Go away!

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.460
Mr. Joe Yabuki...

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.260
"Mr."? Get away from me, creep!

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:43.460
I hate glitzy gold-plated bastards like you more than anything!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:44.470
Now get lost!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:50.270
Yeah, you heard him! Bro Joe's right! Now get lost!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.560
And don't you dare come back, you glitzy bastard!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.930
Yeah, asshole!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:58.940
<i>For God's sake...</i>

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.470
Get lost! Get lost!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.920
And don't you ever drive across Namida Bridge ever again!

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.910
Get lost!

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.840
What do we do now, Henry?

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.840
What else? We'll just have to use our last resort.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.840
Last resort?

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.850
I, Henry the Hyena, will make Carlos an offer he can't pass up.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.860
I'm going out for a bit.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:50.360
Going to Shiraki Gym?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:54.370
Yeah. We gotta get the paperwork done as soon as we can.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:55.870
I'll join you!

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.710
I can do this myself!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:58.910
You keep training!

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.460
Hey, quit making a fuss about training!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.460
I've gotta get out of here from time to time...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.300
Besides, I'm a little worried about Carlos.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.010
You're beyond help. You just can't settle down.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.140
Can't settle down, huh?

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:16.310
I'm feeling exactly the same as I did when my match with Rikiishi was scheduled.

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:21.020
I can jump rope, punch the sandbag, and hit the punching ball all I like,

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.610
but I can't help but feel like I'm wasting my time.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.570
The only thing I can do then is go see my opponent.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.530
I hear Carlos is doing public sparring at Shiraki Gym today.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.280
That's what I want to see.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.000
Fine. Just shut up and follow me.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.290
Hey, why don't we take the company car?

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:43.050
Hey! What if you get in an accident before your match?

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.260
Hah! I wish this thing was fast enough to get into an accident.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:47.180
Now, get on in.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.300
What am I gonna do with you?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:55.980
Are you sure that van's gonna be okay?

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:59.320
Well, the van's one thing, but I'm more worried about Joe's driving!

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.570
That doesn't look good at all...

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.200
I hope Bro Joe's okay...

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:26.250
Well, looks like there's a big crowd here!

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:31.340
Carlos has been the center of attention ever since he KO'd Tiger Ozaki with one punch.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:34.010
This is just the kind of crowd his public sparring match would draw.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.560
So Carlos is a star now...

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.010
And why would a star want to cancel a match with me?

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.350
I don't know.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.980
Just park the van already.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:44.940
Sure... but I don't see any...

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:45.480
Oh, found one!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.280
Hey, that space ain't big enough!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.240
Oh, it'll do fine!

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.170
Joe, I have no part in this!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.340
Hey, don't sweat it!

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.800
Now we better hurry before we miss the public sparring match!

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:21.810
Hello, everyone...

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.310
Well, looks like everyone's here now!

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:26.860
So what's up with Carlos?

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.770
Is the public sparring over?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.150
Actually, it was cancelled.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.230
Cancelled? But why?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.160
Nobody knows.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.370
I did catch a glimpse of Carlos,

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.290
but instead of his usual happy playboy self,

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.740
he looked so pale I barely even recognized him!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.210
I see.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.750
So that would mean it's true that he's scared of me.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.750
What? Scared of you?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.750
Yeah! He wants to cancel our match out of fear!

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:52.180
You're kidding!

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.970
Carlos would never be afraid of a match with you!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.760
No, it's certainly possible.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.020
Otherwise...

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.760
No, that's the only possibility!

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.140
Ridiculous!

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.150
Like fighter, like chairman, I guess!

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.690
You said it! Now let's get going! This is absurd!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:11.100
We didn't come here to hear Tange Gym's bullshit!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.490
Looks like your weird talk drove them all away.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.670
What? Then what am I supposed to do?

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.730
Up until now you've been telling me my opponent is Joe Yabuki,

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:48.190
but today you say it's world champion José Mendoza...

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.980
What is going on here, Miss Yohko?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.240
I cannot give you an answer.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.570
As I see it, they're trying to take you away from me,

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.450
by luring you with money and the championship belt.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.870
You're wrong! I don't mean to steal Carlos from you!

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:06.290
I just want him to take his first chance at the world title!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.500
All his hard work has been for this day alone!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.300
He's right, Carlos. You have to make up your mind.

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.840
Then even more money than we have here,

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:19.050
as well as the championship belt held by José Mendoza, pictured there, will be yours!

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:23.560
This is your chance to repay the favor to Robert, who took you out of the slums!

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.190
Then you can race down the sunny highway together!

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:28.560
You can rise out of the worst slum in Venezuela,

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:32.230
and lay claim to the greatest glory and wealth in the world!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.320
What'll it be, Carlos?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.410
Carlos!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.140
Joe?

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.480
J-Joe...

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:19.900
Carlos?

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:20.900
Carlos!

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.270
Carlos!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.270
<i>Carlos!</i>

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.400
Just watch me, Joe.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.650
These are the punches that you will taste firsthand!

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.700
Carlos! You're not going to...

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:00.690
Carlos!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:06.040
Robert, Henry, I know I've caused you so much trouble, but I've made up my mind.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:09.000
I must fight Joe Yabuki, even if it costs me the Championship Belt!

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.660
That is what I live for!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.380
Carlos...

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.170
Carlos!

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:07.810
Now then, Tange-san...

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:09.010
Apologies for the wait.

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:11.980
Let's handle that paperwork before they change their minds.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:13.810
Yes, good thinking.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:16.850
Now I'm looking forward to their match!

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.200
Looking forward to their match, huh?

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:25.700
Those fucking boxing fanatics!

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:27.120
Well, all right.

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:28.950
If I have the time to spare,

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:31.540
I'd love to watch these uncrowned emperors fight.

00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:41.160
The wild beasts clash in the square jungle!

00:24:42.130 --> 00:24:44.170
The fatal bell has rung in Joe and Carlos' match!

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:47.170
As Noriko and the children cheer him on,

00:24:47.590 --> 00:24:49.270
and Yohko quietly watches over them,

00:24:50.170 --> 00:24:55.140
Joe exerts his final ounce of power against his new rival, Carlos!

00:24:55.140 --> 00:24:58.640
Joe attempts to overcome this endless duel and move on!

00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:00.140
Joe's eyes shine!

00:25:01.190 --> 00:25:07.610
Now, as Joe fights with all the power he has to seize a bright future,

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:09.110
which way is tomorrow!?
